Numerical
The examples are restricted to the scales of 2, 10 because of their importance to electronic computers.

Note that the octal scale is a power of the binary sale. In fact, an octal digit corresponds to a plot of binary digits. Then, binary arithmetic may be used whenever a number either is to be inverted to the octal scale or is given in the octal sale and is to be converted to some other scale.

