Observe that in both examples above, octahedral arithmetic is used as an intermediate step to convert, according to (II), the given number to the binary scale. If, instead, the given number is first converted to the binary scale, then binary arithmetic may be applied directly to convert, according to (I), the given number from the binary scale to the scale desired.

